  "description": "Use when turning a video's compiled evidence into a standalone reader-first article that gives a non-viewer approximately the same understanding and experience as watching the video: one controlling idea, a concrete mechanism/argument chain, examples and demos the reader can picture, visual-first explanations where they help, honest boundaries, and a natural source entry. Not for chapter-by-chapter notes, coverage dumps, encyclopedias, or papers.",
